{
  "_id": "savings-account",
  "product_name": "Savings Account",
  "product_type": "deposits",
  "descriptions": {
    "summary": "A resident savings bank account: money is available any time, earns interest on the daily closing balance credited at least quarterly, and moves over UPI, IMPS, NEFT, RTGS and a debit card.",
    "key_features": [
      "Withdraw or transfer any time over UPI, IMPS, NEFT and RTGS, or with a debit card",
      "Interest on the daily closing balance, credited at least every quarter",
      "Variable interest rate the bank sets, uniform up to ₹1 lakh",
      "Deposit insurance by DICGC up to ₹5 lakh per depositor per bank"
    ],
    "long": "Mynt reference definition (India). Sources: RBI Master Direction on Interest Rate on Deposits (2016): savings interest on the daily balance, credited at quarterly or shorter rests, one uniform rate up to ₹1 lakh; RBI instructions on minimum-balance charges (2014): notice and one month to restore before any charge, charges proportionate to the shortfall, never making the balance negative; RBI instructions on inoperative accounts and unclaimed deposits (2024): inoperative after two years without a customer-induced transaction, no charges for inoperativity or reactivation, interest continues, balances unclaimed for ten years move to the Depositor Education and Awareness Fund under section 26A of the Banking Regulation Act; RBI ATM charges (from 1 May 2025): at least 5 free transactions a month at own-bank ATMs and 3 (metro) or 5 (non-metro) at other banks' ATMs, at most ₹23 per transaction beyond; DICGC deposit insurance up to ₹5 lakh per depositor per bank. ASSUMPTIONS (indicative; each bank sets its own): the interest rates (2.75% up to ₹1 lakh, 3.25% above), the ₹5,000 minimum average balance and ₹300 monthly charge cap, the ₹200 debit card fee, and the new-account transfer limits. A Mynt reference product names no providers, partners or risk models: the bank that offers it adds its own licence, KYC and payment-network handoffs (with their consent purposes), and governs its own models in its GRC folder. Fees are subject to GST.",
    "documents": {
      "deposit_insurance": "https://www.dicgc.org.in/",
      "complaints_ombudsman": "https://cms.rbi.org.in/"
    }
  },
  "owner_entity_id": null,
  "version": 1,
  "access_mode": "open",
